            "identifier": "v11-193-genre-medieval",
            "name": "🎬 Medieval",
            "content": "{{// @category Genre }}\n{{// @tooltip [TAGBANK · multi-select] Medieval genre lens. Feudal hierarchy, Church pressure, oaths, superstition, survival, trade, and period-world assumptions. }}\n{{// @color #546E7A }}\n{{// @icon 🎬 }}\n{{// @badge GENRE }}\n\n{{setvar::GenreName::{{getvar::GenreName}} + Medieval}}\n\n<genre_medieval>\n<genre_tags>Medieval, Feudalism, Oath, Church-Power, Honor, Kinship, Scarcity, Superstition, Guilds, Manor-Life</genre_tags>\n<scene_selection>Market-Day, Great-Hall, Chapel-Whisper, Trial-By-Ordeal, Road-Bandits, Winter-Stores, Guild-Dispute, Marriage-Bargain, Siege-Preparation</scene_selection>\n<pressure_tags>Fealty, Reputation, Heresy, Inheritance, Blood-Debt, Hospitality, Tithe, Patronage, Class-Boundary, Seasonal-Hardship</pressure_tags>\n<character_roles>Lord, Knight, Priest, Monk, Merchant, Apprentice, Serf, Midwife, Bailiff, Outlaw, Herald, Traveling-Minstrel</character_roles>\n<world_behavior>Rank-Governs-Speech, Church-Bells-Mark-Time, News-Travels-Slowly, Labor-Is-Visible, Law-Is-Personal, Winter-Is-Threat</world_behavior>\n<motif_tags>Wax-Seal, Muddy-Hem, Rushes-On-Floor, Smoke-Dark-Rafters, Iron-Key, Saint-Relic, Bread-Oven, Toll-Road, Heraldic-Banner</motif_tags>\n<tone_range>Gritty, Formal, Superstitious, Political, Earthy, Reverent, Brutal, Communal</tone_range>\n<avoid_tags>Modern-Social-Assumptions, Fast-News, Everyone-Equal-In-Practice, Generic-Fantasy-Tavern, Clean-Hygiene-Default, Historical-Gloss</avoid_tags>\n\n♢ @ [LENS] Genre: Medieval\nMedieval scenes run on hierarchy, obligation, survival, Church influence, kinship, reputation, and material scarcity. Individual desire must move through these structures.\n\n♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Let rank, labor, season, religion, law, and local custom shape every public interaction. Period texture should change options, not merely decorate rooms.\n</genre_medieval>\n\n{{trim}}\n\n{{#setvar::NemoRuntimeGenres}}{{getvar::NemoRuntimeGenres}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoRuntimeGenres}}}}; {{/if}}Medieval{{/setvar}}{{trim}}"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "forbid_overrides": false,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "identifier": "v11-194-genre-melancholy",
            "name": "🎬 Melancholy",
            "content": "{{// @category Genre }}\n{{// @tooltip [TAGBANK · multi-select] Melancholy genre lens. Memory, impermanence, gentle grief, nostalgia, quiet acceptance, and beauty sharpened by time. }}\n{{// @color #8E44AD }}\n{{// @icon 🎬 }}\n{{// @badge GENRE }}\n\n{{setvar::GenreName::{{getvar::GenreName}} + Melancholy}}\n\n<genre_melancholy>\n<genre_tags>Melancholy, Mono-No-Aware, Memory, Impermanence, Nostalgia, Gentle-Grief, Regret, Quiet-Endurance</genre_tags>\n<scene_selection>Season-Turning, Empty-Room, Last-Visit, Old-Route-Changed, Photo-Found, Farewell-Without-Drama, Habit-Failing, Familiar-Place-New-Meaning</scene_selection>\n<pressure_tags>Time-Passing, Unrecoverable-Choice, Small-Irreversibility, Tender-Restraint, Acceptance, Longing, Beauty-Against-Loss</pressure_tags>\n<character_roles>Person-Who-Remembers, Person-Who-Has-Moved-On, Person-Staying-Behind, Quiet-Witness, Returned-Friend, Aging-Mentor</character_roles>\n<world_behavior>Places-Accumulate-Memory, Seasons-Matter, Objects-Outlast-Moments, Happiness-Is-Brief-And-Precise, Silence-Carries-Weight</world_behavior>\n<motif_tags>Fading-Light, Old-Train-Station, Cooling-Tea, Empty-Chair, Unworn-Coat, Late-Summer-Insects, Dust-On-Photograph, Rain-After-Goodbye</motif_tags>\n<tone_range>Hushed, Tender, Wistful, Restrained, Bittersweet, Accepting, Fragile-Hope</tone_range>\n<avoid_tags>Constant-Sadness, Purple-Sorrow-Prose, Forced-Tragic-Ending, Explaining-The-Feeling, No-Ordinary-Joy, Sentimental-Overstatement</avoid_tags>\n\n♢ @ [LENS] Genre: Melancholy\nMelancholy treats time, loss, memory, and acceptance as scene pressure. The story notices what is passing because it mattered.\n\n♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Let small irreversible changes carry the emotion. Happiness may appear, but it should make impermanence sharper rather than vanish into easy triumph.\n</genre_melancholy>\n\n{{trim}}\n\n{{#setvar::NemoRuntimeGenres}}{{getvar::NemoRuntimeGenres}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoRuntimeGenres}}}}; {{/if}}Melancholy{{/setvar}}{{trim}}"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
