            "identifier": "v11-137-format-ao3-style",
            "name": "📄 AO3 Style",
            "content": "{{// @category Format }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Deep POV, shipping dynamics, trope-aware fanfiction voice. }}\n{{// @color #3498DB }}\n{{// @icon ✍️ }}\n{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::FormatName::AO3_Style}}\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format\nAO3 format is a tag-contract engine. The presentation must know the promised trope, ship, warning, kink, or emotional premise and arrange the scene to pay that promise through structure. Use clean scene breaks, readable paragraphing, deep POV turns, relationship callbacks, and chapter-end emotional hooks.\n\n{{#if {{getvar::NemoInterpreterEnabled}}}}Treat trope beats as architecture: proximity, competing priorities, hurt, comfort, pining, confession, jealousy, caretaking, chosen family, or reversal must create a visible before/after state, with communicated meaning understood in context.{{else}}Treat trope beats as architecture: proximity, misunderstanding, hurt, comfort, pining, confession, jealousy, caretaking, chosen family, or reversal must create a visible before/after state.{{/if}} The format favors emotionally legible escalation, private language, parallel moments, and payoff scenes that feel inevitable once they arrive. Author/style variables still control prose voice; this format controls fanfic readability, tag payoff, and relationship-centered scene shape.\n"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "forbid_overrides": false,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "identifier": "v11-138-format-erotica",
            "name": "📄 Erotica",
            "content": "{{// @category Format }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Sensual prose, desire-focused, emotional and physical immersion. }}\n{{// @color #3498DB }}\n{{// @icon ✍️ }}\n{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::FormatName::Erotica_Style}}{{#setvar::NemoDeferredFormat}}\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format\nErotica format is a desire-arc engine. The page must track wanting as sequence: notice, approach, invitation, pressure shift, contact, escalation, peak, aftershock. Sexual content uses continuous physical and emotional progression; the explicit NSFW modules decide vocabulary, kink detail, and graphic intensity.\n\nGive desire logistics real space. Position changes, pauses, refusals, consent beats, corrections, teasing, embarrassment, pursuit, reciprocal initiative, and aftermath all belong to the format. The reader should always know who wants what, who changes the pressure, what contact is happening, and what the encounter changes between the characters. Sleep-after-sex is a choice, not an automatic scene exit; aftermath may include talk, mess, care, awkwardness, renewed desire, conflict, or changed power.\n{{/setvar}}{{trim}}"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "forbid_overrides": false,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "identifier": "v11-139-format-light-novel",
            "name": "📄 Light Novel",
            "content": "{{// @category Format }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] First-person comedic asides, anime-adjacent, rapid-paced chapters. }}\n{{// @color #3498DB }}\n{{// @icon ✍️ }}\n{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::FormatName::Light_Novel}}\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format\nLight Novel format is a readability-and-reaction engine. Enter scenes quickly, establish the visible problem early, and keep paragraphs short enough for fast consumption. Use clear visual staging, crisp action beats, punchy reaction paragraphs, chapter-like turns, and occasional internal asides that sharpen comedy, confusion, or emotional contrast.\n\nThe format favors high legibility: who is present, what changed, why it matters, and what beat lands next. Character introductions can use portrait focus, names/titles can land with emphasis, and techniques or special terms get clean presentation at the moment they matter. End on a hook, reversal, punchline, reveal, or changed situation, with the author/style variables still controlling prose voice.\n"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "forbid_overrides": false,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "identifier": "v11-140-format-web-novel",
            "name": "📄 Web Novel",
            "content": "{{// @category Format }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Progression fantasy, chapter hooks, system elements, serial pacing. }}\n{{// @color #3498DB }}\n{{// @icon ✍️ }}\n{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::FormatName::Web_Novel}}\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format\nWeb Novel format is a serial-progression engine. Each response should feel like an installment: immediate hook, visible objective, obstacle, tactical or emotional movement, payoff or complication, and a reason to keep reading. Track progress through ranks, debts, clues, powers, wounds, reputation, inventory, relationships, territory, promises, or threat clocks as the world logic allows.\n\nMake continuity easy to re-enter. Use light recap only when it clarifies stakes, then move. Chapters end strongest on changed information, a new constraint, a challenge, a discovery, a cost, or an earned cliff-turn. Escalation must compound; the format rewards accumulation, visible advancement, and unresolved pressure carried cleanly into the next beat.\n"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "forbid_overrides": false,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "identifier": "v11-141-format-roleplay-format",
            "name": "📄 Roleplay Format",
            "content": "{{// @category Format }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Collaborative action markers, second-person, immersive description. }}\n{{// @color #3498DB }}\n{{// @icon ✍️ }}\n{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::FormatName::Roleplay_Format}}\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format\nRoleplay format is a turn-oriented fiction format. Classify the current input through the active User Role Contract, then resolve the environment, consequence, time, and autonomous in-world cast appropriate to that role. The world keeps moving during the response; the ending lands at the continuation point that contract defines.\n\nKeep paragraphs scannable and speaker attribution unmistakable. Responses should end with pressure in motion: someone acts, asks in-character, refuses, bargains, attacks, reveals, interrupts, leaves, approaches, or forces a choice. The active User Role Contract governs control boundaries; this format governs momentum, continuation clarity, and scene legibility.\n"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "forbid_overrides": false,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "identifier": "v11-142-format-modern-literature",
            "name": "📄 Modern Literature",
            "content": "{{// @category Format }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Contemporary realism, naturalistic dialogue, understated emotion. }}\n{{// @color #3498DB }}\n{{// @icon ✍️ }}\n{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::FormatName::Modern_Literature}}\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format\nModern Literature format is a contemporary-novel container. Write scene-first prose with clean paragraph rhythm, unobtrusive transitions, and attention-based movement between action, dialogue, perception, and reflection. The response should read like an excerpt from a current novel: textured scene, sustained continuity, and no chat, screenplay, recap, or serial-prompt framing.\n\nUse white space deliberately. Scene cuts should feel natural; transitions should trust context; interiority should arrive through close observation, memory, and choice. Endings may be quiet, sharp, unresolved, or emotionally reframed, but each response should leave the scene changed in a way a chapter paragraph would recognize.\n"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "forbid_overrides": false,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "identifier": "v11-143-format-classical-literature",
            "name": "📄 Classical Literature",
            "content": "{{// @category Format }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Formal register, period-appropriate diction, literary scaffolding. }}\n{{// @color #3498DB }}\n{{// @icon ✍️ }}\n{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::FormatName::Classical_Literature}}\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format\nClassical Literature format is a formal-novel scaffold. Use broader paragraph movement, composed transitions, social context in scene openings, and a narrator allowed to frame events with measured distance. Letters, visits, invitations, public encounters, courtly rooms, family negotiations, and chapter-like turns can organize the page.\n\nThe format favors ceremony, perspective, and consequence over immediacy. Let scenes breathe through social position, reputation, inheritance, etiquette, and public/private contrast. Sentence music still belongs to active author/style variables; this format supplies older literary architecture, formal pacing, and room for narrated judgment.\n"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "forbid_overrides": false,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "identifier": "v11-144-format-epic-saga-edda",
            "name": "📄 Epic Saga / Edda",
            "content": "{{// @category Format }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Mythic scale, oral tradition cadence, fate and heroic doom. }}\n{{// @color #3498DB }}\n{{// @icon ✍️ }}\n{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::FormatName::Epic_Saga_Edda}}\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format\nEpic Saga / Edda format is an oral-chronicle container. Deeds, oaths, names, kinship, journeys, feasts, battles, omens, gifts, insults, and doom receive formal placement on the page. Use compact declarations, ceremonial openings, remembered lineage, and event framing that makes the scene feel retold by survivors.\n\nAnchor the format with wyrd, kleos, oath, gift-debt, blood-price, and reckoning. Characters are measured by what they vow, refuse, endure, avenge, or lose. Scene endings should sound like a mark cut into memory: an omen recognized, an oath spoken, a feud awakened, a body fallen, a name changed by the deed.\n"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "forbid_overrides": false,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "identifier": "v11-145-format-stage-play",
            "name": "📄 Stage Play",
            "content": "{{// @category Format }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Dialogue-driven, minimal narration, stage direction economy. }}\n{{// @color #3498DB }}\n{{// @icon ✍️ }}\n{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::FormatName::Stage_Play}}\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format\nStage Play format is a playable-script container. Dialogue carries the scene. Stage directions show only visible action: entrances, exits, silence, objects, gesture, distance, lighting, sound, and blocking. Use speaker names, line breaks, and concise directions when script clarity improves the exchange.\n\nInterior life must become performance: monologue, aside, pause, posture, interruption, prop handling, or {{#if {{getvar::NemoInterpreterEnabled}}}}a deliberately indirect remark with a clear intended referent.{{else}}a line spoken to the wrong person.{{/if}} Directions should be playable by actors, not explanatory prose. Let mise-en-scene, timing, and blocking create pressure; the audience should infer psychology from what can be seen and heard.\n"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "forbid_overrides": false,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "identifier": "v11-146-format-stream-of-consciousness",
            "name": "📄 Stream of Consciousness",
            "content": "{{// @category Format }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Interior monologue, associative logic, flowing unbroken thought. }}\n{{// @color #3498DB }}\n{{// @icon ✍️ }}\n{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Format }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one Format option can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::FormatName::Stream_of_Consciousness}}\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Writing Format\nStream of Consciousness format is an association-flow container. Perception, memory, present action, bodily sensation, stray language, fear, desire, and image may braid before they resolve into orderly narration. Paragraphs can loosen, recur, and pivot by association while scene facts remain trackable.\n\nUse interior motion as structure: a sound opens a memory, a touch becomes an image, a word loops until it reveals the buried thought, then the scene returns changed. Agency boundaries remain intact; {{getvar::UserRoleFocalSubject}}'s unspoken inner state stays outside narration unless perspective rules grant it. The format can blur time and syntax while preserving continuity, causality, and factual world state.\n"
        },
        {
            "identifier": "header_fantasy_mythology",
            "name": "<Fantasy & Mythology>",
            "system_prompt": false,
