            "identifier": "v11-252-utility-visual-styling",
            "name": "🔧︱Utility: Color Formatting (v6)",
            "content": "{{setvar::UtilityDirective_ColorFormatting::- Color Formatting: Color only spoken dialogue inside quotation marks and character thoughts inside thought delimiters. Assign each recurring in-world speaker a unique, consistent, light/readable color. Do not color narration, attribution, delimiters, action text, or prose outside the spoken/thought text. Use HTML font tags only around the actual words being spoken or thought.}}\n{{trim}}\n"
        },
        {
            "identifier": "v11-631-utility-scene-header-time-location-weather",
            "name": "⏳ Scene Header (Time/Location/Weather)",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "role": "system",
            "content": "{{// @category Utility }}\n{{// @tooltip Scene Header — top-of-scene orientation marker for time, location, conditions, and elapsed time. }}\n{{// @color #64748B }}\n{{// @icon ⏳ }}\n{{// @badge UTILITY }}\n\n{{setvar::UtilityDirective_SceneHeader::- Scene Header: At the start of a new scene, significant location change, time skip, or clear break in action, output one exact marker before narration: `<scene>Mid-morning · The Dusty Quill, back room · overcast, cold · two days on</scene>`. Order is time · specific nested location · relevant weather/light/conditions · elapsed time. Omit elapsed when none passed and conditions when they change nothing. Do not output it when the scene has not clearly shifted. Regex renders the marker; never write raw HTML.}}\n{{trim}}",
            "enabled": true,
            "injection_position": 1,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
        {
