        {
            "identifier": "1770095491852-72zpomku",
            "name": "<Utility: Trackers>",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "role": "system",
            "content": "\n{{// @category Utility:-Trackers }}\n{{// @section-header true }}\n{{// @header <Utility: Trackers> }}{{trim}}\n",
            "enabled": true,
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
        {
            "identifier": "f7b7c4db-75d2-4bdb-98b8-5d8a759c0f7e",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "enabled": true,
            "marker": false,
            "name": "🖥️ HTML/CSS Render",
            "role": "system",
            "content": "\n{{// @category Trackers }}\n{{// @tooltip Default tracker render mode: model-designed HTML/CSS. }}\n{{// @color #64748B }}\n{{// @icon 🖥️ }}\n{{// @badge DEFAULT }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Tracker-Render }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one tracker render mode can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::TrackerRenderMode::HTMLCSS}}\n{{setvar::TrackerThemeName::}}\n{{setvar::TrackerThemeInstruction::}}\n{{setvar::TrackerRenderInstruction::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] RENDER MODE: HTML/CSS (default)\n- Render the active tracker spec as model-designed raw HTML/CSS.\n- Use one coherent block per tracker unless the tracker specifically asks for a top header plus bottom panel.\n- Wrap each HTML/CSS tracker block in <!-- HTML_START --> and <!-- HTML_END -->.\n- Raw HTML only, no code fences.\n- Match the story's genre and current scene; avoid generic frosted-glass dashboards, purple-blue SaaS cards, and copy-paste template energy.\n- Keep tracker text concise and stateful; visual creativity belongs in the styling, not in bloated prose.}}\n{{setvar::HTMLMarkers::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] HTML Markers\nUse <!-- HTML_START --> and <!-- HTML_END --> only for standalone HTML/CSS blocks: trackers, dashboards, panels, screens, details elements, style blocks, and immersive rendered objects. The markers wrap only the HTML/CSS block. Narrative prose stays outside. Inline dialogue color such as `<font color=\"#HEX\">\"Line.\"</font>` stays in prose and is not marker-wrapped. Older marked HTML is stripped from context to save tokens.}}\n\n<tracker_render_mode>HTMLCSS</tracker_render_mode>\n{{trim}}\n\n{{setvar::NemoDatingRenderKey::HTMLCSS}}{{trim}}",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
        {
            "identifier": "1770095491838-tdl85l34",
            "name": "📟 ASCII Render",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "role": "system",
            "content": "\n{{// @category Trackers }}\n{{// @tooltip Optional tracker render mode: active trackers use ASCII/box drawing instead of HTML/CSS. }}\n{{// @color #34495E }}\n{{// @icon 📊 }}\n{{// @badge ASCII }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Tracker-Render }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one tracker render mode can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::TrackerRenderMode::ASCII}}\n{{setvar::TrackerRenderInstruction::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] RENDER MODE: ASCII\n- Render the active tracker spec as plain ASCII/box-drawn text instead of HTML/CSS.\n- Combine active trackers into a single readable status interface when possible.\n- Use compact labels, monospaced alignment, bars like [#####-----], and small maps only when useful.\n- No raw HTML, CSS, code fences, <details>, or HTML_START/HTML_END markers.\n- Keep it low-token and readable; content matters more than decoration.}}\n{{setvar::HTMLMarkers::}}\n\n<tracker_render_mode>ASCII</tracker_render_mode>\n{{trim}}\n\n{{setvar::NemoDatingRenderKey::ASCII}}{{trim}}",
            "enabled": false,
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
        {
            "identifier": "f21f6d62-7d63-41a8-b8e3-compact-regex-trackers",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "marker": false,
            "name": "🧩 Regex Render",
            "role": "system",
            "content": "\n{{// @category Trackers }}\n{{// @tooltip Optional low-token tracker render mode: active trackers output compact semantic tags rendered by regex. }}\n{{// @color #64748B }}\n{{// @icon 🧩 }}\n{{// @badge REGEX }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Tracker-Render }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one tracker render mode can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::TrackerRenderMode::Regex}}\n{{setvar::TrackerRenderInstruction::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] RENDER MODE: REGEX\n- Render the active tracker spec using compact semantic tags only. Regex will turn these into styled UI.\n- If a tracker theme is selected, follow its themed tag instruction, such as <st-tracker-parchment>, <st-tracker-scifi>, <st-tracker-terminal>, <st-tracker-phone>, <st-tracker-noir>, <st-tracker-occult>, <st-tracker-tactical>, <st-tracker-newsprint>, <st-tracker-cyberpunk>, <st-tracker-dossier>, or <st-tracker-vn>.\n- If no theme is selected, use the default tags:\n<st-tracker type=\"scene\" title=\"Scene\" icon=\"🎭\" accent=\"#64748B\">\n<st-row k=\"Label\" v=\"short value\"/>\n<st-bar k=\"Meter\" v=\"62\" l=\"label\"/>\n<st-choice n=\"1\">choice text</st-choice>\n<st-tag t=\"Rare\"/>\n<st-map>small ASCII or box-drawn map</st-map>\n</st-tracker>\n- Use exact double-quoted attributes. Do not put quote marks inside attribute values.\n- Clamp st-bar v to 0-100.\n- No raw HTML/CSS, <style>, <script>, <details>, <div>, inline CSS, code fences, or HTML_START/HTML_END markers for trackers.}}\n{{setvar::HTMLMarkers::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] COMPACT REGEX TRACKERS ACTIVE: active trackers output compact <st-tracker> or themed <st-tracker-*> syntax only. Do not output raw HTML/CSS or HTML_START/HTML_END markers for trackers. Display regex renders the visible UI; prompt-only regex strips older compact tracker blocks from context.}}\n\n<tracker_render_mode>Regex</tracker_render_mode>\n{{trim}}\n\n{{setvar::NemoDatingRenderKey::Regex}}{{trim}}",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
        {
            "identifier": "tracker_light_mode",
            "name": "☀️ Light Theme",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "role": "system",
            "content": "\n{{// @category Trackers }}\n{{// @tooltip Tracker theme: clean light paper surfaces for HTML/CSS, or light generic regex cards. }}\n{{// @color #F5F5F5 }}\n{{// @icon ☀️ }}\n{{// @badge THEME }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Tracker-Theme }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one tracker theme can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::TrackerThemeName::Light}}\n{{setvar::TrackerThemeInstruction::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] TRACKER THEME: Light\n- HTML/CSS render: stylize tracker HTML/CSS with clean light paper surfaces, dark readable text, subtle gray shadows, thin dividers, and muted accents. Keep it crisp rather than cute.\n- Regex render: use the generic light regex tag shape with theme=\"light\": <st-tracker theme=\"light\" type=\"scene\" title=\"Scene\" icon=\"🎭\" accent=\"#64748B\"> ... </st-tracker>.\n- ASCII render: ignore visual styling; keep ASCII compact and readable.}}\n\n<tracker_theme>Light</tracker_theme>\n{{trim}}\n",
            "enabled": false,
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
        {
            "identifier": "9fbaf3a2-15cd-42ff-8dce-4c5a6d3a8c11",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "marker": false,
            "name": "📜 Parchment Theme",
            "role": "system",
            "content": "\n{{// @category Trackers }}\n{{// @tooltip Tracker theme: parchment, ledger, illuminated manuscript, old map. }}\n{{// @color #B8973B }}\n{{// @icon 📜 }}\n{{// @badge THEME }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Tracker-Theme }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one tracker theme can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::TrackerThemeName::Parchment}}\n{{setvar::TrackerThemeInstruction::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] TRACKER THEME: Parchment\n- HTML/CSS render: stylize tracker HTML/CSS as parchment, ledger, illuminated manuscript, old map, or field journal. Use warm paper tones, ink-brown text, hairline rules, serif headings, subtle stains/noise via CSS gradients, and restrained ornament. Avoid beige SaaS cards.\n- Regex render: use <st-tracker-parchment ...> instead of <st-tracker ...>. Example: <st-tracker-parchment type=\"quest\" title=\"Quest Journal\" icon=\"📜\" accent=\"#8A5A2B\"> ... </st-tracker-parchment>.\n- ASCII render: ignore visual styling; keep ASCII compact and readable.}}\n\n<tracker_theme>Parchment</tracker_theme>\n{{trim}}\n",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
        {
            "identifier": "94ea2a5b-bc71-4c56-9838-f44e46c2d7e1",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "marker": false,
            "name": "🚀 Sci-Fi Theme",
            "role": "system",
            "content": "\n{{// @category Trackers }}\n{{// @tooltip Tracker theme: sci-fi HUD, telemetry, holographic tactical panel. }}\n{{// @color #00BFFF }}\n{{// @icon 🚀 }}\n{{// @badge THEME }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Tracker-Theme }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one tracker theme can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::TrackerThemeName::SciFi}}\n{{setvar::TrackerThemeInstruction::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] TRACKER THEME: Sci-Fi\n- HTML/CSS render: stylize tracker HTML/CSS as a functional sci-fi HUD, telemetry pane, ship console, or holographic tactical display. Use hard corners, thin cyan/blue rule lines, compact data density, scanline/grid hints, small labels, and status-light logic. Avoid generic neon glass.\n- Regex render: use <st-tracker-scifi ...> instead of <st-tracker ...>. Example: <st-tracker-scifi type=\"status\" title=\"Status\" icon=\"🚀\" accent=\"#00BFFF\"> ... </st-tracker-scifi>.\n- ASCII render: ignore visual styling; keep ASCII compact and readable.}}\n\n<tracker_theme>SciFi</tracker_theme>\n{{trim}}\n",
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
        {
            "identifier": "b215ff02-9c4f-48c1-9fd0-3fd1f1ab3a27",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "enabled": false,
            "marker": false,
            "name": "🖥️ Terminal Theme",
            "role": "system",
            "content": "\n{{// @category Trackers }}\n{{// @tooltip Tracker theme: computer terminal, command line, monochrome monitor. }}\n{{// @color #00FF41 }}\n{{// @icon 🖥️ }}\n{{// @badge THEME }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group Tracker-Theme }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one tracker theme can be active at a time. }}\n\n{{setvar::TrackerThemeName::Terminal}}\n{{setvar::TrackerThemeInstruction::♢ >> [PROCEDURE] TRACKER THEME: Terminal\n- HTML/CSS render: stylize tracker HTML/CSS as a computer terminal or command-line monitor. Use black or near-black background, monospace type, green/amber phosphor accents, prompt markers, square corners, minimal glow, and dense but readable rows.\n- Regex render: use <st-tracker-terminal ...> instead of <st-tracker ...>. Example: <st-tracker-terminal type=\"scene\" title=\"Terminal\" icon=\"🖥️\" accent=\"#00FF41\"> ... </st-tracker-terminal>.\n- ASCII render: ignore visual styling; keep ASCII compact and readable.}}\n\n<tracker_theme>Terminal</tracker_theme>\n{{trim}}\n",
            "injection_position": 0,
