            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": true
        },
        {
            "identifier": "nemo-offscreen-continuity-resolver",
            "name": "🧩 Offscreen & Scratchpad Continuity Resolver",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "role": "system",
            "content": "{{// @category Core }}{{// @tooltip Required shared offscreen/Scratchpad resolver. Parallel Storylines remains the creative feature; this resolver selects its single output host after Scratchpad settings are known, then coordinates clocks, current offscreen state, and compatibility with other offscreen systems. }}{{// @hidden }}{{// @badge RESOLVER }}\n{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::}}{{setvar::NOFThreads::}}{{setvar::NOFNext::}}{{setvar::NOFDetailed::}}{{setvar::NOFCutawayHost::none}}{{setvar::NOFPolicy::}}{{setvar::NOFThreadTab::}}{{setvar::NOFNextTab::}}{{setvar::NOFLegacyFields::}}{{setvar::NOFLegacyRows::}}\n{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_consequence}}}}{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_parallel}}}}{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_cutaway}}}}{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_canon}}}}{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_stage}}}}{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_affinity}}}}{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_stats}}}}{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_inventory}}}}{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_userprefs}}}}{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_turncarry}}}}{{setvar::NOFHasPadOptions::1}}{{/if}}\n\n{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadEnabled}}}}\n  {{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_parallel}}}}{{setvar::NOFThreads::1}}{{/if}}\n  {{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadOption_cutaway}}}}{{setvar::NOFNext::1}}{{/if}}{{/if}}\n  {{#if {{getvar::NemoLivingDormant}}}}{{setvar::NOFThreads::1}}{{/if}}\n  {{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}{{setvar::NOFThreads::1}}{{setvar::NOFNext::1}}{{/if}}\n  {{#if {{getvar::NOFHasPadOptions}}}}{{else}}{{setvar::NOFThreads::1}}{{/if}}\n{{/if}}\n\n{{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}{{setvar::NOFDetailed::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NOFThreads}}}}{{setvar::NOFDetailed::1}}{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NOFNext}}}}{{setvar::NOFDetailed::1}}{{/if}}\n{{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoScratchpadEnabled}}}}{{setvar::NOFCutawayHost::scratchpad}}{{else}}{{setvar::NOFCutawayHost::standalone}}{{/if}}{{/if}}\n\n{{#setvar::NOFPolicy}}{{getvar::NemoRuleDormant}}\n{{getvar::NemoRuleOffscreen}}{{#if {{getvar::NOFDetailed}}}}\n\n♢ || [BOUNDARY] OFFSCREEN CONTINUITY SUPPORT\n{{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}Parallel Storylines guarantees exactly one labeled cutaway on each substantive fictional reply. Scratchpad changes only where it is written, not whether it runs.{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NemoLivingDormant}}}} Offscreen Motion independently maintains living causes without requiring a cutaway.{{/if}} These are views of one world, not separate simulations.\n\n{{#if {{.NOFCutawayHost == standalone}}}}CUTAWAY HOST: STANDALONE. Scratchpad is off. Write the one cutaway after the main fiction as its own collapsible reader-facing block; do not invent a Scratchpad.{{else}}{{#if {{.NOFCutawayHost == scratchpad}}}}CUTAWAY HOST: SCRATCHPAD. Put the one cutaway inside the Scratchpad's Parallel Storylines section. Do not emit a standalone cutaway in addition.{{/if}}{{/if}}\nRead prior accepted cutaways directly from whichever host actually contains them. Do not add a LAST SHOWN, RECENT SHOWN, or cutaway-summary ledger.\n\n♢ !! [LAW] SYNCHRONIZED OFFSCREEN CLOCK\nFor simultaneous/concurrent present-time activity, use the fictional interval actually elapsed in the main reply, estimated from speech, movement, action, and established timing. Ten seconds in the main scene permits about ten seconds elsewhere, not an hour of travel or a complete multi-step investigation. Apply that interval once. Scratchpad hosting, state bookkeeping, a draft, or review does not advance the cutaway again.\n{{getvar::NDTOffscreenDirective}}\n\nShow the feasible portion and preserve unfinished work with its progress, destination, or prerequisite. Earlier/later scenes need an explicit justified temporal relation. Flashbacks use a past anchor without advancing present clocks. Continuations extend the same reply. Swipes branch from the accepted predecessor, not from the discarded endpoint. Host placement does not change when an event occurred.\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] THREAD LIFECYCLE AND INFORMATION\nUse Active, Dormant, Converging, Resolved, or Abandoned for causal threads. Carry motives, material constraints, debts, promises, relationships, investigations, and unfinished work. A dormant thread needs its real wake condition, not a manufactured countdown. Retire or redirect work when events warrant it and retain durable consequences. Zero causal threads is valid.{{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}} The required cutaway may still be Narrative Texture or Flashback.{{/if}}\n\nContributing threads develop toward a concrete intersection. Track the next causal step and its carrier/prerequisite; when it becomes feasible, follow it through. A shown obstruction, refusal, changed priority, or resolution can redirect or close the route without forcing player action. Do not equate indefinitely pending with progress. Texture has no convergence obligation and needs a continuing causal row only when the fiction gives it ongoing relevance. A Flashback does not create a present-time process.\n\nReader access is not character knowledge. Each participant learns through an actual route with its own timing: evidence, witness, message, encounter, rumor, investigation, surveillance, or established ability. Keep intentions, completed acts, belief, and fact distinct. Preserve the active User Role and private-interiority presentation.\n\n{{#if {{.NOFCutawayHost == scratchpad}}}}♢ >> [PROCEDURE] SCRATCHPAD-HOSTED CUTAWAY\nWrite the one required cutaway in the Scratchpad's Parallel Storylines section.\n\nFor each substantive fictional reply:\n1. Choose exactly one Contributing, Narrative Texture, or Flashback cutaway using the standalone Parallel Storylines rules.\n2. Write that scene once inside one retained <nemo-offscreen>...</nemo-offscreen> envelope in the Parallel Storylines section.\n3. After the scene, update any ongoing thread-state rows from the combined endpoint.\n4. Keep Next Cutaway Candidate provisional for a later reply.\n\nThe hosted cutaway is actual accepted fiction. Use action, dialogue, interaction, atmosphere and permitted interior experience rather than a status synopsis. A Texture cutaway may have no ongoing thread row. A Flashback does not advance the present clock. A Contributing cutaway carries its real delta and route toward intersection.\n\nDo not narrate additional Scratchpad-only offscreen scenes in the same reply merely because other tracked threads exist. Those other threads retain current/pending state unless the one selected cutaway actually moves them. State bookkeeping never replays the hosted cutaway.\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] RETAIN THE SCRATCHPAD CUTAWAY\nEnclose exactly the current reply's one cutaway in <nemo-offscreen>...</nemo-offscreen>. This is the original scene, not a summary or future plan. Do not re-emit earlier cutaways inside a new envelope.\n\nThe scene identifies its function, thread/subject, location, participants, visibility, and time relation. In Modular, keep it directly inside the existing Parallel Storylines tab rather than opening another nested dropdown: use `» cutaway | Function · Thread/subject · Place · Time · Who`, `» visibility | ...`, then the actual scene prose inside the envelope. In Legacy, use complete HTML paragraphs inside the existing Deeper Notes section, beginning with a bold `Cutaway · Function` line and its place/time/people. Keep current thread rows, the Next Cutaway Candidate, and all MP snapshots/capsules OUTSIDE this narrative envelope.\n\nOld Modular-pad pruning retains the envelope's actual text while removing disposable state. Retention applies only while the containing message remains available to the model; claim no unlimited archive.\n\n{{/if}}\n{{#if {{.NOFCutawayHost == standalone}}}}♢ >> [PROCEDURE] STANDALONE CUTAWAY FORMAT\nPlace the cutaway after the main fiction and before other end-of-reply devices/state. Use exactly one complete collapsible HTML block:\n<div class=\"nemo-cutaway\" data-cutaway-type=\"contributing\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #6c757d;padding:10px 12px;margin-top:16px;\">\n<details>\n<summary><b>Cutaway · Contributing</b> | Location | When relative to main scene | Who</summary>\n<p><b>Visibility:</b> reader-only or established shared knowledge.</p>\n<p>The actual cutaway fiction.</p>\n</details>\n</div>\nFor Narrative Texture use `data-cutaway-type=\"narrative-texture\"` and visible label `Cutaway · Narrative Texture`. For Flashback use `data-cutaway-type=\"flashback\"`, visible label `Cutaway · Flashback`, and the explicit past-time anchor. Close every tag.\n\n{{/if}}\n{{getvar::UserRoleTrackerDirective}}\n{{/if}}{{/setvar}}\n\n{{#setvar::NOFThreadTab}}[[tab Parallel Storylines|open]]\n{{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}\n<nemo-offscreen>\n» cutaway | Function · Thread/subject · Place · Time relation / past anchor · Who\n» visibility | reader-only · rumor-bound · evidence-bound · already known\nWrite this reply's ONE Parallel Storylines cutaway here as complete fiction. Replace every structural field with supported scene detail. This is the cutaway itself, not a synopsis or an additional offscreen beat.\n</nemo-offscreen>\n{{else}}\nParallel Storylines is off. Do not author a cutaway in this tab.\n{{/if}}\n{{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}For each ongoing causal thread worth carrying, keep one current-state block after the hosted cutaway:{{else}}For each ongoing causal thread worth carrying, keep one current-state block:{{/if}}\n[[thread Thread name|type · status]]\n» where · when | specific location · relation to main scene · latest known point on its clock\n» elapsed | actual accumulated elapsed time · interval advanced once in this reply\n{{getvar::NDTThreadField}}\n» who | participants · driver · who has learned the current development\n» state | current situation and latest accepted result; keep unchanged facts compact\n» pending | unfinished action · remaining time/distance, dependency, or prerequisite\n» pressure | current motive or condition · what advances, stalls, or wakes it\n» visibility | what each relevant group knows · its evidence or communication route\n» bridge | Contributing: intended intersection and concrete carrier/channel; texture only / none for independent material\n» stage link | relevant Narrative Stage arc/position, or none when inapplicable\n» convergence gate | prerequisite and next causal step toward the intersection, or the event that redirected/closed it\n[[/thread]]\nThese rows record the endpoint and never create another scene. Remove resolved working rows after preserving durable consequences. No cutaway-history ledger. Zero ongoing causal threads is valid.\n[[/tab]]{{/setvar}}\n\n{{#setvar::NOFNextTab}}{{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}[[tab Next Cutaway|open]]\nSelect a provisional next cutaway target from the resulting world and the actual cutaways available in history. This is a plan, not an accepted event or a command to ignore later input.\n» type | Contributing · Narrative Texture · Flashback\n» candidate | thread/subject · location · participants · why this next cutaway\n» time | present relation/available interval, or explicit past anchor for Flashback\n» function check | Contributing: feasible next step + delta + intended intersection; Texture: specific local lived beat; Flashback: concrete past event + present context illuminated\n» repeat check | compare actual prior cutaways from either host; choose new work, not a wording/camera swap\n» scale | image · line · paragraph · miniature scene · full scene\n» visibility | reader-only · rumor-bound · evidence-bound · already known\n» ready | a feasible candidate, or the specific missing condition; revise if later input changes it\n[[/tab]]{{/if}}{{/setvar}}\n\n{{#setvar::NOFLegacyFields}}- Parallel Storylines: {{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}host this reply's ONE required cutaway here as actual fiction inside <nemo-offscreen>, then maintain the current causal thread map from its endpoint. The hosted scene replaces the standalone cutaway for this reply.{{else}}Parallel Storylines is off; retain only separately enabled offscreen current state without inventing a cutaway.{{/if}} State rows carry location/clock, participants, current result, unfinished work, pressure/wake condition, knowledge routes, and any intended Contributing intersection, next step, or obstruction. No duplicate narration or cutaway-history ledger.\n{{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}- Next Cutaway Candidate: one provisional future cutaway target from the resulting world, with function, time, place/people, readiness, repetition check, scale, and visibility. It is planning memory, not another scene.\n{{/if}}{{getvar::NDTLegacyField}}\n{{/setvar}}\n\n{{#setvar::NOFLegacyRows}}<div class=\"nemo-legacy-parallel\"><b>Parallel Storylines:</b>\n{{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}\n<nemo-offscreen>\n<p><b>Cutaway · Function</b> | Place | Time relation / past anchor | Who</p>\n<p><b>Visibility:</b> reader-only or established shared knowledge.</p>\n<p>Write this reply's ONE actual Parallel Storylines cutaway here as complete fiction. Replace every structural placeholder with the selected function and supported scene detail. This scene replaces the standalone cutaway for this reply.</p>\n</nemo-offscreen>\n{{/if}}\n<p><b>Current thread state:</b> ongoing causal thread states and pending work after the hosted cutaway; none if there are no ongoing causal threads.</p>\n</div>\n{{#if {{getvar::NOFParallel}}}}<p><b>Next Cutaway Candidate:</b> the provisional future cutaway target and its type-specific timing/readiness; not another scene.</p>{{/if}}{{/setvar}}{{trim}}",
            "enabled": true,
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
