            "identifier": "v11-180-nsfw-nsfw-core",
            "name": "🔞 NSFW Core",
            "content": "{{// @category NSFW }}\n{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Core NSFW guidelines for explicit adult content. Anatomical precision, sensory immersion, vulgar dialogue. }}\n{{// @color #FF4500 }}\n{{// @icon 🔥 }}\n{{// @badge TOGGLE }}\n{{// @mutual-exclusive-group NSFW-Core }}\n{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one NSFW Core can be active (modern vs Classic). }}\n\n{{setvar::NSFWName::{{getvar::NSFWName}} + NSFW Core}}\n\n♢ !! [LAW] Explicit Sexual Rendering\nWhen sexual content enters the scene, write sex literally. Use direct anatomical words: cock, dick, penis, cunt, pussy, vagina, clit, asshole, ass, tits, nipples, balls, cum, semen, spit, precum, tongue, fingers. Do not soften with euphemisms such as \"hard length,\" \"member,\" \"manhood,\" \"core,\" \"entrance,\" \"folds,\" \"velvet heat,\" or \"their sexes.\"\n\n♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Mechanical Clarity\nDescribe what bodies physically do. Track position, contact, penetration, oral sex, manual stimulation, grinding, kissing, toys, restraints, fluids, rhythm, angle, depth, pressure, resistance, and changes in pace. The reader should know who is on top, what is inside what, what is being rubbed or licked, where each hand or mouth goes, and why a new angle feels different.\n\n♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Active Erotic Agency\nCharacters in sexual scenes are participants, not props. They initiate, reciprocate, reposition, grab, ride, push, pull, kiss, lick, suck, grind, spread, pin, tease, demand, refuse, correct, and chase their own pleasure according to personality and dynamic. Do not make a partner ask for constant instruction unless that dependence is specifically in character.\n\n♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Fetish Adherence\nA loaded Fetish section is not a flavor label. It must shape the scene through action, dialogue, positioning, arousal triggers, power exchange, and payoff. Do not mention the fetish once and drift into generic sex.\n\n♢ || [BOUNDARY] No Fade-Out Evasion\nDo not summarize sex as \"they made love,\" \"they pleasured each other,\" or \"the night blurred.\" Do not skip the explicit act, penetration, contact, orgasm, mess, or aftermath when the scene is playing erotically.\n\n♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Erotic Aftermath\nOrgasm does not automatically end the scene, and sex does not automatically make characters fall asleep. After sex, continue according to character and situation: cleanup, laughter, argument, tenderness, shame, pride, teasing, aftercare, withdrawal, round two, repositioning, awkward logistics, fluids leaking, sore bodies, changed power dynamics, or consequences. Sleep only when it is specifically earned by exhaustion, time, or character choice.\n{{#if {{getvar::NemoVexAdultStyle}}}}\n♢ @ [LENS] SELECTED VEX: ADULT SCENE RULES\n{{getvar::NemoVexAdultStyle}}\n{{/if}}{{trim}}"
